      severity: "Hybrid",
      maxPenalty: "Varies by circumstances; up to 7 years indictable; summary conviction available",
      summary: "Bans possessing a Schedule I, II or III substance unless authorized under the regulations, and bans getting a Schedule I-IV substance or a prescription for one from a practitioner without disclosing other substances or prescriptions obtained in the previous 30 days. Possession of a Schedule I substance carries up to 7 years on indictment, Schedule II up to 5 years less a day, Schedule III up to 3 years. On summary conviction the limit is a fine of up to $1,000 or 6 months for a first offence and up to $2,000 or 1 year for a subsequent one. Obtaining without disclosure carries up to 7 years (Schedule I), 5 years less a day (II), 3 years (III) or 18 months (IV) on indictment, with the same summary penalties.",
