      severity: "",
      maxPenalty: "",
      summary: "Protects a person who calls for emergency medical or law enforcement help for a life-threatening reaction to a psychoactive substance, and anyone else at the scene when help arrives, from being charged or convicted of simple possession under s. 4(1) where the evidence came from the call or from staying at the scene. It also bars charges for breaching pre-trial release or probation conditions related to a s. 4(1) offence in the same circumstances, and deems those conditions (including conditional sentence and parole conditions) not to be violated.",
